      "reference": {
        "answer": "The data includes summaries from recent investor calls for ABB India Limited, which provide insights into the company's performance and strategic focus:\n\n- **Earnings Call (August 7, 2026)**:\n  - ABB reported a **50% year-on-year increase** in orders and a **21% rise in revenue** for Q2 2026.\n  - The operational EBITA was **12.8%**, with profit after tax (PAT) growing by **8%**.\n  - The order backlog stood at **INR 11,900 crores**, with no slow-moving orders.\n  - Significant contributions came from sectors such as **renewables, data centers, and infrastructure**.\n  - The company achieved an **85% reduction in GHG emissions** and was recognized as **India's Most Sustainable Company** in the Capital Goods sector.\n  - An interim dividend of **INR 90 per share** was declared, reflecting a **50% payout ratio** from normal earnings.\n  - Management expressed confidence in maintaining operational efficiency despite challenges from rising material costs and forex volatility.\n\n- **Investor Presentation (July 31, 2026)**:\n  - The presentation reiterated the **50% increase in orders** received, totaling **INR 4,363 crore**, and a **21% rise in revenue** to **INR 3,559 crore** compared to Q2 CY2025.\n  - The order backlog was noted at **INR 11,898 crore**, with robust demand across sectors including **metals, mining, and cement**.\n  - Profit after tax increased by **8%** to **INR 370 crore**, while operational EBITA rose by **23%**.\n  - ABB's commitment to sustainability was highlighted, achieving an **85% reduction in Scope 1 and 2 GHG emissions** year-to-date compared to a 2019 baseline.\n  - The company faced challenges from **commodity price increases** and **currency fluctuations** impacting profitability.\n\nThese summaries reflect ABB's strong performance and strategic focus on sustainability and operational efficiency.",
